.TH PYCDLIB-NAMESPACE-DIFF 1 "Nov 2026" "pycdlib-namespace-diff"

.SH NAME
pycdlib-namespace-diff - read-only report comparing the ISO9660, Joliet, Rock Ridge, and UDF namespaces in an ISO

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pycdlib-namespace-diff [\-\-json] <iso-file>

.SH DESCRIPTION
A hybrid ISO can carry up to four independent views of the same medium: the
original ISO9660 namespace, the Joliet namespace, the Rock Ridge namespace,
and (when present) a UDF namespace.  A path that is spelled identically in two
of these namespaces does not necessarily resolve to the same on-disk bytes.
This tool walks each namespace separately and produces a read-only report that
records, for every entry, its original on-disk name, the location of its name
record (a directory record or UDF File Identifier Descriptor), and the data
extent range(s) the name points at.

The report correlates the views on their display paths and on the underlying
inode they resolve to.  It distinguishes hard links (several names for one
allocation) from independent copies that happen to hold byte-identical
content, and flags paths whose names resolve to different payloads.  Each
finding states whether the difference comes from the name mapping or from the
data source.  No namespace is treated as authoritative, so disagreements are
never hidden by selecting a "best" namespace.

If one namespace cannot be enumerated, the failure is recorded and the
findings from the namespaces that still work are reported unchanged.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the report as JSON instead of the default human-readable text.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was produced and every present namespace enumerated without error.
.TP
.B 1
The ISO could not be opened.
.TP
.B 2
The report was produced, but at least one namespace failed to enumerate; the
other namespaces are still reported.

.SH SEE ALSO
pycdlib-explorer(1), pycdlib-extract-files(1), pycdlib-genisoimage(1)
